  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "If the {only}reading you {ever}do is the novel or {magazine}, the {speed}at which you read— {probably}does not {matter}very much.But if you have to read a great {deal}for study, you will {appreciate}the benefits of being {able}to read more {quickly}.Here are some tips to help {improve}your reading speed.",
      "cn": "如果你 <u> 一直 </u> 以来 <u> 只 </u> 读小说或 <u> 杂志 </u> 的话，那阅读 <u> 速度可能 </u> 并不那么 <u> 重要 </u> 。但是，如果你必须为了学习而大 <u> 量 </u> 阅读，你就会 <u> 意识到能够快速 </u> 阅读的好处。以下是一些帮助你 <u> 提高 </u> 阅读速度的小技巧。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "{before}you {open}the {book}, make {sure}that you are comfortable.You need a {seat}which {support}your back and the book should be at the right {distance}from your {eye}.Keep the room {cool}rather than {warm}to {avoid}feeling {sleepy}.",
      "cn": "<u> 在 </u> 你 <u> 打开书之前 </u> ， <u> 确保 </u> 自己处于舒适的状态。你需要一个能 <u> 支撑 </u> 背部的 <u> 座位 </u> ，并且书与 <u> 眼睛 </u> 的 <u> 距离 </u> 要适中。室内不要太 <u> 暖和 </u> ， <u> 凉爽 </u> 一点更好，以 <u> 免 </u> 感到 <u> 困倦 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Spend a few {minute}looking {through}the book.Look at the {table}of contents, the {preface}, the {chapter} {heading} , etc.This will help you to decide whether you {really}need to read the whole book or only certain parts of it.Ten minutes spent in this way could save you quite a lot of time in the long {run}.",
      "cn": "先花几 <u> 分钟 </u> 时间浏览一下这本书。看看目录、 <u> 前言 </u> 、 <u> 章节标题 </u> 等。这将帮助你决定是否 <u> 真的 </u> 需要阅读整本书，还是只需阅读其中的某些部分。从长远来看，花十分钟这样做可以为你节省大量的时间。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "If you decide that you need to read the whole book, decide how much you can read at a {time}.This depends on the {type}of book you are reading.A {history}book, which may {contain}the facts in {story}form, will be easier to read than one dealing with {scientific}{subject}.In the {former} {case} , you may be able to read a chapter.In the {latter}, you may only be able to read one page.",
      "cn": "如果你决定需要阅读整本书，确定一下你一 <u> 次 </u> 能读多少内容。这取决于你阅读的书籍 <u> 类型 </u> 。 <u> 历史 </u> 类书籍可能 <u> 包含 </u> 以 <u> 故事 </u> 的形式讲述的事实，因此比探讨 <u> 科学题材 </u> 的书籍更容易阅读。在 <u> 前一种情况 </u> 下，你或许能够读完一章。而对于 <u> 后者 </u> ，你可能只能读完一页。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Always keep a {pencil}and {paper} {beside} you.Make a note of any page that is of special {importance}.Note also the facts important for your {purpose}as well as {anything}that leads you to {further}research.You don't have to write these things in {detail}.It is {enough}to write down the page {number}and one or two words as a reminder.",
      "cn": "始终 <u> 在身边 </u> 准备好 <u> 铅笔 </u> 和 <u> 纸 </u> 。记下任何特别 <u> 重要 </u> 的页面。还要记下对你的阅读 <u> 目的 </u> 来说重要的事实，以及 <u> 任何 </u> 能引导你进行 <u> 进一步 </u> 研究的 <u> 内容 </u> 。你不必 <u> 详细 </u> 地记录这些内容。只要写上页 <u> 码 </u> 和一两个词作为提醒就 <u> 足够 </u> 了。"
    }
  ],
